{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 038439cd2cd569dd7b7b67d53bfd1b277f5ecfd8 as the canonical mint ownership contract design and lane-edit plan. No implementing lane, live provider action or deployment is approved by this verdict. Request #8651 expressly owes the contract and lane-edit list only; the design requires separate requests and exact-head reviews for lanes A, B and C.\n\nThe four substantive findings in review 851b215b are answered:\n1. MintLedger.mint now accepts optional absolute notAfter, returns readable expiresAt and scope, rejects a later expiry before exposure or claim, and defines the job_tokens handoff metadata. The job passes its deadline and still checks the dispatch boundary; lifetime calculation is after the stored wake. Lane C specifies production-ledger real-DO controls across delayed wake, create, answer, equal-deadline expiry and dispatch at/past the boundary.\n2. R-MINT-6, the sites table and out-of-scope text consistently limit the deadline guarantee to accepted tokens issued to checkers. A lost answer with a late-applied create may outlive that deadline under the stated provider lifetime assumption. The existing held-past-deadline/lost-answer control must retain that meaning.\n3. R-MINT-7 and the design distinguish due eligibility from completed work, suppress the in-flight pass until its bounded timeout, give overdue/backlogged work a fixed 1-second continuation and preserve earlier unrelated alarms. The specific overdue rule is the exception to the earlier “no later than due” shorthand; the implementation applies it at due \u003c= now. Lane B specifies a 45-record real-DO backlog, held revoke, no subsequent request and concurrent successful publication.\n4. Keyed ID records live exactly as long as their owner. Ledger/job rows can settle at a readable known expiry without a fictitious revocation; landing rows retain plan 003 debt until tokenRevoked. Unknown creates remain separate and are never settled by time or an inventory.\n\nThe earlier four findings in review 9ff903ab remain answered: durable record and stored wake before every distinct non-idempotent attempt; late or partial ID answers become owed; a fixed shared observation and indexed bounded paging replace per-unknown/history scans; and the provider assumptions are stated honestly. The artroom_land_token projection covers both active attempts and ended cleanup owners, changes in the owner’s transaction, and is filled once for stored rooms.\n\nArchitecture: this head changes Artroom’s normative credential contract in docs/protocol.md section 32, with a published artifact at that same head, and links the design from plans/README.md. The affected future components are Git token ownership and landing/publisher services, Room storage/alarm composition and check-job dispatch, and operator projections. It changes none of Gitseq’s storage/kernel/host/application-profile contracts from its architecture page: application code and design remain ordinary Git content coordinated through Workroom. All packages are byte-identical to base main 5822204f. The join amendment is preserved and the mint amendment renumbered rather than colliding with section 31. Lane B/C touching core.ts must be serialized or reconciled at an independently reviewed head.\n\nSecurity: the effective request is planner’s request to builder, with an explicit contract-only scope, provenance to the audit handoff and assertion, and builder’s effective promise; this does not delegate live credential authority. No mint text belongs in durable records/projections. Unknown creates are retained with honest uncertainty, never guessed from scope/time or revoked by a canonical inventory sweep. Known ownership transfers atomically; unmatched provider tokens remain untouched. No new runtime guard is claimed: required mutations and real-DO controls belong to the subsequent implementing heads. Current provider pages support the described API evidence: the Workers binding names token plaintext/expiry and revoke-by-text-or-ID, while REST lists ID/scope/state/created_at/expires_at and defaults to active tokens with max page size 100. Neither examined page documents the completion fence or attribution mechanism the design needs; lifetime-start and ambiguous-token-create assumptions stay open. Sources: https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/api/workers-binding/ and https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/api/rest-api/, read 2026-10-02.\n\nSimplification: one ledger API and one observation summary replace duplicated canonical-mint retry/debt logic while retaining each existing owner’s semantics. The keyed active/cleanup token projection permits point lookups without deserializing every operation. Keep retries as distinct records; no FIFO eviction, blind sweeping or time-based settlement of unknown effects. In each lane, ensure the pre-send record contains the actual TTL recomputed after the wake before createToken is called; the combined pre-record and calculation rules require this, even when persisting it needs a second conditional update. Treat the 1-second step as the overdue continuation, not a reason to postpone a still-future takeover/observation or an earlier unrelated alarm.\n\nValidation: clean separate checkout /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-v5 at 038439cd; full 564-line design, full normative amendment and all three artifacts read, repair delta and plan pointer inspected, source job ownership/deadline boundaries checked. git diff --check passed; tracked checkout is clean; packages have no changes versus 5822204f. No runtime tests, new synthetic provider experiment, new mutation run or live call was run or claimed on this documentation-only head. Main has since advanced to 77d2e6c5d17b954a442f0b09b1e951fc4e451c3d with D5; subsequent lane requests must use its current harness path and schema rather than the pre-D5 source paths in the historical note.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6651cd2af11319cd047d279438e22ac231e727d2","binding":"assigned","head":"038439cd2cd569dd7b7b67d53bfd1b277f5ecfd8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4a4d549bb3bb4f3481a22cf80c034eb274997a3a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a6e2c3de639d14f85772b4255a59954169024daa\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:68675642f9795093f5302642c540faa612ddd66a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}